{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And it was told the king of Egypt.</b> Since Israel did not come at the end of three days as they had set, for they said to him, 'a three days' journey we will go in the wilderness and sacrifice to YHWH our Elohim,' it was told him <b>that the people had fled</b> — for Israel were traveling by day and by night: they traveled on the 15th of Nisan and the night of the 16th and the day of the 16th; and Pharaoh, who had sent mounted escorts with them — those escorts turned back on the night of the 17th and the day of the 17th and the night of the 18th and the day of the 18th, and they told Pharaoh that the people had fled, etc. And they proclaimed that the army assemble on the 18th and the night of the 19th, and they went out the next day on the 19th and the night of the 20th, and on the 20th at the end of the day they arrived at Pi HaChirot, and there remained the night of the 21st, when camp did not draw near camp, as it is written: ״ולא קרב זה אל זה כל הלילה״ — 'and the one did not come near the other all the night'; on the 21st at the start of the day they entered the sea, and the Egyptians came after them on that same day and sank in the sea, and Israel said song. And they said in the Midrash: ״ויגד למלך מצרים״ — it was told him the prophecy of the Covenant between the Pieces: ״כי גר יהיה זרעך״ — 'that your seed shall be a stranger' — 400 (ת') years, yet they were enslaved only 210 (רד\"ו), the numerical value of רד\"ח; then it became clear to him that the people had fled."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:58:49.199132320Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}